ENTRY            G4122   20260708   20261124   20261124       G061
SUBENT        G4122001   20260708   20261124   20261124       G061
BIB                 11         29
TITLE      Product yields for the photofission of 241Am by
           bremsstrahlung photons with energy of 12.5 MeV
AUTHOR     (O.O.Parlag,V.V.Pyskach,A.I.Lengyel,A.N.Gomonai,
           E.V.Oleinikov,I.V.Pylypchynets)
INSTITUTE  (4UKRIEP)
REFERENCE  (J,VAT/I,,(3/163),38,2026)
           #doi:10.46813/2026-163-038
FACILITY   (MICRT,4UKRIEP) M-30 microtron
INC-SOURCE (BRST) To generate bremsstrahlung, a tantalum
           converter (rectangular plate with dimensions of 100 x
           50 mm and a thickness of 1 mm) was used, located at a
           distance of 22 mm from the output window (material -
           titanium, thickness - 50 mu-m) of the electron
           ejection unit. The filter for residual electrons and
           secondary photoneutrons (a cylindrical single crystal
           of lithium tetraborate (Li2B4O7) with a diameter of
           30 mm and a height of 19 mm) was installed close to
           the Ta converter perpendicular to the beam axis.
DETECTOR   (HPGE,GELI) Semiconductor HPGe and Ge(Li) detectors
           with volumes of 150 and 100 cm3, respectively, were
           used for the spectrometric measurements.
SAMPLE     The active 241Am layer, 11 mm in diameter, was
           deposited on a disc-shaped substrate (diameter 24 mm,
           thickness 1 mm) made of 12X18H10T stainless steel.
           The isotopic content of 241Am in the sample was > 99%.
METHOD     (ACTIV) Induced beta-delayed gamma-activity measured.
STATUS     (APRVD) Approved by O.Parlag
HISTORY    (20260708C) UkrNDC
           (20260708R) Data received from O.Parlag
ENDBIB              29
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           32
